{"kind":"component","id":"1140f52d-bf6c-46e7-9552-29c4b9957777","type":"6e2b9c41-8d57-4a3f-b1e0-7c94d2a6f815","name":"Linear Buckling Analysis (Alpaca4d)","nick":"Buckling","desc":"Finds the load factors at which the model buckles under its loads, lowest first - the first is the critical load factor α_cr - and the shapes it buckles into.\nThe loads are those of the assembled model at load factor 1, as one step of Run Analysis applies them. The analysis is linear: elastic, about the undeformed shape, with the axial forces of a first-order analysis.\nFor it every beam gets a PDelta transformation. Beam elements buckle in bending only: lateral-torsional and torsional buckling need warping, which they do not have.\nConnect the assembled model, or an analysed one for the buckling of the model it was analysed from - Section Optimiser's last design, say. Feed the buckled model to Nodal Displacements or View Results: its steps are the buckling modes, step 0 the first.","box":[1342,608,112,64],"pivot":[1400,640],"inputs":[{"id":"ca91dba4-68fa-4e66-a2c6-3362b9b2152f","name":"AlpacaModel","nick":"AlpacaModel","box":[1344,610,41,20],"src":["e3f52b41-6383-47e2-b554-eef1e5cc6bff"]},{"id":"d8aa83eb-beb3-4e52-ad9c-93d224a5ccd8","name":"Buckling Modes","nick":"Buckling Modes","box":[1344,630,41,20],"src":[]},{"id":"4a36e471-c34a-4442-924d-69613e430804","name":"Divisions","nick":"Divisions","box":[1344,650,41,20],"src":[]}],"outputs":[{"id":"eee127a6-71f9-42dd-93a7-683010eaaba5","name":"AlpacaModel","nick":"AlpacaModel","box":[1415,610,37,20],"src":[]},{"id":"a3894a02-c803-4a51-becf-edc61c6cf282","name":"Load Factors","nick":"Load Factors","box":[1415,630,37,20],"src":[]},{"id":"bd18b9f4-7678-48d9-9eb6-6f0f86e70c9f","name":"log","nick":"log","box":[1415,650,37,20],"src":[]}]},
